.TH ROULETTE 1 "November 2026" "roulette 2.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
roulette \- a zero-edge roulette table in your terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B roulette
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B roulette \-\-commands
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B roulette
seats you at a single-zero (European) roulette table. Place bets, watch the
ball land, and get paid from a persistent bankroll in
\fB~/.roulette/state.json\fR (you start with 100 chips).
.PP
The house has no edge. Landing on \fB0\fR is a \fBSUPER SPIN\fR: bets on 0 pay
36:1, and every other bet rides a re-spin on 1\(en36 only. A bet covering
\fIk\fR of the numbers 1\(en36 therefore wins with probability exactly
\fIk\fR/36 at the standard 36/\fIk\fR\(mi1 payout, so every bet has an
expected value of exactly zero.
.PP
At the table, type a target and a chip count in either order to place a bet
(e.g. \fBred 10\fR, \fB10 red\fR, \fB17 5\fR); when two numbers could be read
either way, say \fICHIPS\fR \fBon\fR \fITARGET\fR (e.g. \fB5 on 17\fR). Press
Enter to spin. Enter with no bets is a free spin that moves no chips;
\fBrebet\fR repeats
your last bets. \fBbets\fR, \fBundo\fR, \fBclear\fR, \fBtable\fR,
\fBhistory\fR, \fBstats\fR, \fBbeg\fR, \fBtip\fR, \fBhelp\fR and \fBquit\fR
are also understood.
.PP
A randomly chosen croupier (Gaston, Céleste, Lorenzo, Penelope, ...) comments on your bets and results, calls out the
Martingale when you keep doubling after losses, and accepts tips
(they have no effect on the odds). Roughly one spin in 200 the ball escapes
before being re-thrown, and straight-up hits get a small fireworks show.
None of this changes any outcome.
.SH BREAKING THE BANK
Each run starts with 100 chips. Reach 1000 to break the bank and win the run;
a new run then starts with 100 chips and a new croupier. On the fair wheel the
chance of that is exactly 10%, whatever you bet.
.PP
The croupier can be bribed with \fBtip\fR. Each chip tipped is +2.5% luck, up to
30%: the chance a losing spin is rigged your way. Luck fades by a tenth of each
tip per betting spin, so a tip is gone after 10 spins. The pit boss notices a
rig with probability 1% per 3 chips won, doubled for every bust earlier in the
run; if caught, your bets are seized and an honest croupier takes over. Tipping about one chip a spin while betting 25 chips
raises the chance of breaking the bank to roughly 30%.
.PP
\fBswap_table\fR (or \fB\-\-swap\-table\fR) moves you to another table with a
different croupier and resets your luck to zero. For 5 spins after a pit-boss
bust, the pit boss won't let you move.
.SH BETS
.TP
.B red black odd even low high
Even money, 1:1. \fBlow\fR is 1\(en18, \fBhigh\fR is 19\(en36.
.TP
.B d1 d2 d3 col1 col2 col3
Dozens and columns, 2:1.
.TP
.IR N " (0\(en36)"
Straight up, 35:1 (36:1 on 0, also called \fBgreen\fR).
.TP
.BR 17/18 ", " 17/20
Split, 17:1.
.TP
.B 7-9
Street, 11:1.
.TP
.B 1/2/4/5
Corner, 8:1.
.TP
.B 1-6
Six line, 5:1.
.SH COMMAND WHEEL
With \fB\-\-commands\fR (or \fB\-\-russian\fR), roulette instead spins a reel
of harmless, read-only shell commands, lands on one and runs it with
\fBbash \-c\fR. Each command is a colored pocket (red, black, a green
"loser", or a magenta "super spin" wildcard that turns entropy into red or
black), so you can bet on it with \fB\-\-bet\fR and \fB\-\-on\fR
red|black|green|jackpot. A red/black bet that lands on a green pocket gets a
second-chance super spin.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-commands
Spin the wheel of harmless commands instead of the roulette table.
.TP
.B \-\-russian
Command wheel plus a \(lqrussian roulette\(rq slot. If the spin lands on it,
every file and folder in the current directory is moved to the trash. Opt-in,
recoverable (desktop trash, not \fBrm\fR), and confirmed before deleting.
.TP
.B \-\-table
Show the betting layout and every payout, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-bet " CHIPS"
Wager \fICHIPS\fR on a single spin instead of sitting down at the table.
.TP
.BI \-\-on " TARGET"
What to bet on (see \fBBETS\fR). Defaults to \fBred\fR.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Spin, but move no chips (command mode: run nothing).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pick ", " \-f ", " \-\-fast
Skip the spin animations.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List every command on the command wheel and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-wheel
Command mode: keep the reel on screen after it lands.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECS"
Command mode: seconds to allow the winning command to run (default: 15).
.TP
.B \-\-pray
Pray to the roulette gods. They reply according to how your night is going;
the odds are unchanged.
.TP
.B \-\-swap\-table
Move to another table with a different croupier; your luck starts over at zero.
.TP
.BI \-\-tip " CHIPS"
Tip (bribe) the croupier; see \fBBREAKING THE BANK\fR. With \fB\-\-bet\fR, the tip is
paid before the spin. A tip of 0 is accepted, deeply resented, and lowers your
luck by 2.5%; with negative luck the croupier spoils that share of winning spins.
.TP
.B \-\-beg
Beg the house for chips \(em the only way to earn them back. While broke the
house spots you 100 chips, with escalating sass; beg with money
in hand and it mocks you instead. The house bails you out only twice per run:
beg a third time and you are thrown out of the casino and lose the game,
which then starts over with a new run of 100 chips.
.TP
.B \-\-stats
Show the bankroll, record, realized return and recent numbers, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-reset
Reset the bankroll to 100 chips and clear stats.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colors.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " N"
Seed the random generator for a reproducible spin.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, colors are disabled (same as \fB\-\-no\-color\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.roulette/state.json
Bankroll, statistics and recent numbers.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B roulette
Sit down at the table.
.TP
.B roulette \-\-bet 5 \-\-on 17
One spin, 5 chips straight up on 17.
.TP
.B roulette \-\-commands
Spin the command wheel and run the winner.
.SH AUTHOR
roulette contributors.
